1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,760
Decision Layer is evidence-driven enterprise software evaluation. Its two modules, Visitor Lab

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:11,520
and Evaluation Workspace, help buyers and their agents understand and verify product

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,000
fit.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,133
Enterprise software websites make buyers do the translation. Optimizing for more shortlists

5
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:24,267
can even reward false claims. In our existing Pulse benchmark, the misleading

6
00:00:24,267 --> 00:00:30,400
variant had the highest shortlist rate. Our guard blocked its contradicted claims.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:35,000
These are offline agent results, not human conversion measurements.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,636
Here is FlowBridge, a fictional integration vendor. Our buyer needs EU hosting,

9
00:00:42,636 --> 00:00:50,273
SSO, and a workflow that recovers without duplicate records. The buyer confirms

10
00:00:50,273 --> 00:00:57,909
the requirements before the workspace evaluates them. EU hosting is documented. SSO

11
00:00:57,909 --> 00:01:05,545
is unknown. We preserve that uncertainty. Switching to the finance view changes

12
00:01:05,545 --> 00:01:10,000
the emphasis while keeping the same facts.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,119
Now we click Prove it. This executes real code against local mock

14
00:01:17,119 --> 00:01:24,237
CRM and warehouse systems. It injects a temporary failure and retries using

15
00:01:24,237 --> 00:01:31,356
the same idempotency key. The assertions check successful delivery, failure recovery, and

16
00:01:31,356 --> 00:01:38,475
exactly one destination record. A passing run demonstrates this bounded scenario. It

17
00:01:38,475 --> 00:01:45,000
does not certify the real vendor, and SSO still needs verification.

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,347
Next we simulate a competitor source update. RelayWorks moves EU hosting to

19
00:01:52,347 --> 00:01:59,694
a quote-only Enterprise plan. The change stays pending until an operator approves

20
00:01:59,694 --> 00:02:07,041
it. After approval, the comparison explains the new plan restriction and uncertain

21
00:02:07,041 --> 00:02:14,388
cost. The earlier report remains frozen, so the buyer can inspect what

22
00:02:14,388 --> 00:02:15,000
changed.

23
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,455
The same approved evidence is available to a buyer agent. Its output

24
00:02:20,455 --> 00:02:25,909
includes citations, and the application checks its decision against deterministic rules. For

25
00:02:25,909 --> 00:02:31,364
this EU brief, the correct answer remains needs verification. When cloud inference

26
00:02:31,364 --> 00:02:36,818
is unavailable, the screen explicitly says Rule-based evaluation. Visitor Lab measures correctness

27
00:02:36,818 --> 00:02:40,000
across the homepage and structured evaluation context.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,500
Presentation experiments lead into the Evaluation Workspace. Visitor Lab checks whether agents

29
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:49,000
reach accurate decisions. Evidence, test outcomes, and decision rules stay grounded as

30
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,500
the interface and source material change. Coframe integration is a future connection,

31
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,000
not a shipped claim.

32
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Decision Layer. A living website that demonstrates product fit.
